div class="pulse:flex pulse:flex-col pulse:gap-6"
  p class="pulse:text-sm pulse:text-neutral-600"
    ' Primitive palettes have no utility classes. Reach them through a semantic name.
  - palettes.each do |name, swatches|
    section
      h2 class="pulse:mb-2 pulse:text-lg pulse:font-bold pulse:text-neutral-900"
        code class="pulse:font-mono" = name
      div class="pulse:grid pulse:grid-cols-10 pulse:gap-1"
        - swatches.each do |swatch|
          div class="pulse:flex pulse:flex-col pulse:justify-end pulse:h-20 pulse:p-2 pulse:rounded pulse:text-xs pulse:font-mono" style="background-color: #{swatch.hex}; color: #{swatch.ink}" title="#{name}-#{swatch.shade}"
            span = swatch.shade
            span = swatch.hex
